{"version":1,"ops":[{"type":3,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1507876853,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDMzNjM2NDQwNQ==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/1897#issuecomment-336364405"},"message":"Keep in mind that DataLad only sees the (unique) values on index generation. Afterwards they are scattered across the documents in the search index. So what you are aiming for needs a new kind of query, and/or more info stored in the index, and/or a separate dump of unique values (at index generation time).\n\nFrom my POV this has little (if anything) to do with `search`, but it is as you say: 'some meta-data \"analysis\"'. The appropriate metadata representation for this is the aggregated metadata in the dataset, not the (possibly vastly inflated) representation that the search is running on.\n\nThere are a ton of possibilities what could be done with the metadata, ranging from summary stats, visualization, export to a different format. I think those should be their own thing and not seep into the core commands.","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1509272771,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDM0MDI1MTc4Mw==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/1897#issuecomment-340251783"},"message":"No disagreement...closing.","files":null},{"type":4,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1509272771,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDExOkNsb3NlZEV2ZW50MTMxNTQ3OTIwOA=="},"status":2}]}